From: Esteban Urrutia <esteuwu@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: alpha-pll: preserve enabled Lucid Ole PLLs

Backport the enabled-PLL guard from the upstream display handoff fix.
The TB520FU uses Lucid Ole display PLLs and can still scan out the
firmware framebuffer while the clock driver registers.

Upstream: 2295d6a84179bfe853244c8ef26d6f54b29959cb
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260713-sm8450-qol-dispcc-v3-3-56fd05822270@proton.me/

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-alpha-pll.c
@@ -2373,6 +2373,15 @@
 {
 	u32 lval = config->l;
 
+	/*
+	 * Preserve PLLs left running by the bootloader: disabling them here
+	 * can lock up an RCG still driving the firmware display.
+	 */
+	if (trion_pll_is_enabled(pll, regmap)) {
+		pr_debug("Lucid Ole PLL is already enabled, skipping configuration\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
 	lval |= TRION_PLL_CAL_VAL << LUCID_EVO_PLL_CAL_L_VAL_SHIFT;
 	lval |= TRION_PLL_CAL_VAL << LUCID_OLE_PLL_RINGOSC_CAL_L_VAL_SHIFT;
 	clk_alpha_pll_write_config(regmap, PLL_L_VAL(pll), lval);
